Description:
 ros-jazzy-legged-controllers - Model of legged robot
Changes:
 ros-jazzy-legged-controllers (3.5.0-2026.08.22.10.32) noble; urgency=high
 .
   * Publish the estimator markers from a realtime publisher
     The visualization built a MarkerArray, filled in frame ids and namespace
     strings and called publish() directly, in the 500 Hz update. That is
     roughly thirty allocations plus a middleware handoff per cycle on the
     control thread, while the odometry publisher beside it already used a
     RealtimePublisher with trylock.
     Build the constant fields once and update only the pose and scale.
     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <mailto:noreply@anthropic.com>
   * Do not fabricate NaN joint samples on a failed interface read
     JointSensors read through LoanedStateInterface::get_value, which is
     deprecated and returns quiet_NaN when its try-lock times out. That NaN
     went straight into the generalized position, pinocchio, the Kalman
     filter and out again as a joint command, so a moment of lock contention
     manufactured exactly the failure this series is chasing. It is also the
     only remaining NaN source upstream of the finiteness check.
     Read through get_optional instead and hold the previous sample for any
     joint that fails, which is what IMUSensor already does, and warn. The
     samples are now members rather than three vectors allocated per cycle.
     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
   * Fix operator precedence in getColorFromId
     id - 1 % 7 parses as id - (1 % 7). With eight or more contacts the cast
     target left the enum's value range, which is undefined; below that it
     agrees with the intended expression, so nothing rendered changes here.
     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <mailto:noreply@anthropic.com>
   * Check the state interface and command interface write results
     Both call sites discarded a bool that reports a real failure, and
     LoanedCommandInterface::set_value is even marked [[nodiscard]].
     - assign_loaned_state_interfaces leaves the component's interface list
     short when a name does not match, after which JointSensors would index
     it out of bounds. Fail activation instead. get_ordered_interfaces
     appends without clearing, so both components are released on either
     failure path: otherwise the partial list dangles once
     controller_manager reclaims the loans, and a retry appends on top and
     can never succeed again. controller_manager refuses activation when a
     requested interface is missing, so this is defence in depth.
     - set_value try-locks and returns false on timeout; swallowing that
     silently left the joint at its previous command with no indication.
     Warn, throttled, on the failure branch only.
     - Bound setCommands by the number of claimed interfaces, and take the
     command vector by reference rather than by value, which was allocating
     on every call from the control loop.
     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
   * Contributors: qiayuanl
